<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExchangeBusiness> linkml:description "Applies when calculating the number of days between two dates the count includes only stock exchange business days." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExchangeCode> linkml:description "The identifier follows the symbology set by the exchange which lists the asset." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExchangeRate> linkml:description "Denotes a rate to convert one currency or other measure of value to another. Foreign Exchange rates are represented in decimals, e.g. {amount, unitOfAmount, PerUnitOfAmount} = [1.23, USD, GBP] = USD 1.23 for every 1 GBP." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExchangeTradedFund> linkml:description "Denotes an investment fund consisting of stocks, bonds, and/or other assets that is passively managed and traded on a stock exchange." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Exchangeable> linkml:description "Specifies a debt security that can be converted to equity in a company other than the issuing company." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Executed> linkml:description "The position has been executed, which is the point at which risk has been transferred." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExecutedInBelgium> linkml:description "The Agreement was executed outside of Belgium" .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExecutedOutsideBelgium> linkml:description "The Agreement was executed outside of Belgium" .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExecutingBroker> linkml:description "The (generally sell-side) organization that executed the trade; the price-making party." ;
    linkml:meaning "http://www.fpml.org/coding-scheme/party-role-4-0#ExecutingBroker"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExecutingEntity> linkml:description "Entity executing the transaction.  If the transaction is executed directly by the reporting party, it will be the reporting party.  If it is executed by an execution agent or an affiliated party on behalf of the reporting party, it will be that affiliate or agent." ;
    linkml:meaning "http://www.fpml.org/coding-scheme/party-role-4-0#ExecutingEntity"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExecutionAgent> linkml:description "The (generally buy-side) organization that acts to execute trades on behalf of an investor. Typically this is an investment manager or asset manager, and also makes the investment decisions for the investor. If required, a separate InvestmentDecision role can be specified to distinguish that the party making the investment decision is different." ;
    linkml:meaning "http://www.fpml.org/coding-scheme/party-role-4-0#ExecutionAgent"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExecutionFacility> linkml:description "The facility, exchange, or market where the trade was executed. Synonym: Swap Execution Facility, Designated Contract Market, Execution Venue." ;
    linkml:meaning "http://www.fpml.org/coding-scheme/party-role-4-0#ExecutionFacility"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExecutionWithinFirm> linkml:description "Person within the firm who is responsible for execution of the transaction." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Exercise> linkml:description "A cash flow associated with an exercise lifecycle event." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExerciseNoticeReceiverPartyCancelableProvision> linkml:description "Specifies the party to which notice of a cancelable provision exercise should be given." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExerciseNoticeReceiverPartyExtendibleProvision> linkml:description "Specifies the party to which notice of a extendible provision exercise should be given." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExerciseNoticeReceiverPartyManual> linkml:description "Specifies the party to which notice of a manual exercise should be given." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExerciseNoticeReceiverPartyOptionalEarlyTermination> linkml:description "Specifies the party to which notice of a optional early termination exercise should be given." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Exercised> linkml:description "The (option) contract has been exercised." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExercisingParty> linkml:description "The party that gives notice of exercise. Per 2000 ISDA Definitions, Section 11.1. Parties, paragraph (d)." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ExercisingPartyPays> linkml:description "If optional early termination is applicable to a swap transaction, the rate, which may be a bid or ask rate, which would result, if seller is in-the-money, in the higher absolute value of the cash settlement amount, or, is seller is out-of-the-money, in the lower absolute value of the cash settlement amount." .

