<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Weighted> linkml:description "The arithmetic mean of the relevant rates in effect for each day in a calculation period calculated by multiplying each relevant rate by the number of days such relevant rate is in effect, determining the sum of such products and dividing such sum by the number of days in the calculation period." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/WeightedAverage> linkml:description "Denotes a value as the Volume Weighted Average of prices effective on the Pricing Date." .

<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Wertpapier> linkml:description "Issued by the Institute for the Issuance and Administration of Securities in Germany (Securities Information), the Wertpapierkennnummer (WKN, WPKN, WPK or simply Wert) consists of six digits or capital letters (excluding I and O), and no check digit. It is used to identify German securities." .

