<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Seller> linkml:description "A counterparty in a trade, which performs in one of the following capacities: 1) it transfers or agrees to transfer in the future an instrument or title to that instrument in exchange for payment, 2) it writes a derivatives instrument such as an option or a swap in which it provides risk protection to the buyer. This does not refer to the broker/dealer or other organization on what is typically called  the 'Sell side'; for that, see the 'Executing Broker' role. Corresponds to 'Seller' as defined in certain regulations such as ESMA MiFID II/MIFIR RTS 22 field 16.",
        "Seller of the legal title to the financial instrument.",
        "Specifies that only the option seller has the right to exercise." ;
    linkml:meaning "http://www.fpml.org/coding-scheme/party-role-4-0#Seller"^^xsd:anyURI .

